      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is similar to how shared lib dependencies among cc_* libraries are handled. Soong installs everything, but it emits LOCAL_SHARED_LIBRARIES as well so that the module which depended on isn\u0027t dropped from file_list.txt.\n\nLOCAL_SOONG_JNI_LIBS_* is very complex and tricky. The reason it works is it sneakily adds the jni libs to `.INSTALLED` list of the apk [1]. I don\u0027t want to bring the complexity back. \n\nOn folding: I didn\u0027t intentionally squashed this CL in the revert^2 CL, in order to highlight the forward fix. But since you ask, I did it.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/make/core/install_jni_libs_internal.mk;drc\u003dd203e12f20b5b7dc843f4c910739b2c21e5e8667;l\u003d84",
